# Copy this file to .env for local `go run .`. .env is gitignored.
PORT=8080
LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG

# Required in both modes: the Paprika account. Use the test account while developing.
PAPRIKA_EMAIL=you@example.com
PAPRIKA_PASSWORD=change-me

# Required in HTTP mode: one or two comma-separated SHA-256 hashes (64 hex
# characters each) of the bearer token. This example is the hash of the
# throwaway token "local-dev-token"; generate your own (see README.md).
MCP_TOKEN_SHA256=0cd48eed49739dfdd99efaef37d251aae5a80866e5954763c6597943fff5ce9b

# Optional: extra allowed Origin values, comma-separated. Requests with no
# Origin header are always allowed; any other unknown Origin is rejected.
# MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com

# Optional: register write tools. Defaults to false.
# PAPRIKA_WRITES_ENABLED=false

# Optional: the Paprika request limiter, a token bucket. The defaults loaded a
# full library on a real account; try 45 if stalls appear. Tune them from the
# requests_last_12s count logged at each stall. The burst must be greater than
# 2, the reserve kept for tool calls.
# PAPRIKA_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=50
# PAPRIKA_REQUEST_BURST=4

# Optional: keep a snapshot of the recipe index so restarts skip the full load.
# INDEX_STORE is none (default), filesystem, or s3. A bad value stops startup.
# INDEX_STORE=none
# INDEX_FILE_PATH=./recipe-index.json.gz
# INDEX_S3_BUCKET=
# INDEX_S3_KEY=paprika-mcp-go/recipe-index.json.gz
# INDEX_S3_ENDPOINT=
